Yes. FastAPI allows multiple body parameters, so you can send an `item` object and a `user` object together. The JSON body must wrap each object under a key that matches the parameter name, e.g.:
```json
{
  "item": {"name": "Foo", "description": "The pretender", "price": 42.0, "tax": 3.2},
  "user": {"username": "dave", "full_name": "Dave Grohl"}
}
```
